<%# `Admin::Ui::MediaPickerComponent`'s grid: `Admin::MediaController#index`
    with `picker=1`, rendered without a layout into the picker's own
    `<turbo-frame id="media-picker-grid">` -- the toolbar's form and the page links
    below stay inside that frame (Turbo scopes a frame's own forms and links to it),
    so searching, choosing a segment and paging never navigate the editor underneath
    the modal, and the dialog never closes or jumps. `picker` rides along in the
    toolbar's form (hidden field) and in the pagination links (`list_params`, which
    names it among the keys to keep), so every later request comes back here, not to
    the full Media module page. The toolbar is the Media screen's own
    (`Admin::MediaLibrary::ToolbarComponent`, `picker: true`), the tiles the grid's
    (`pick: true`). The place this answer is of, and whether a `folder` that named
    nothing was answered as All media, is one hidden element INSIDE the frame
    (`#media-picker-place`): Turbo moves only a response frame's children into the
    live frame, never its attributes, so the picker's script reads the place, its
    name and `data-media-place-gone` (to forget a remembered place) from there.

    The frame's body is the picker's two columns (the card's D12), laid out
    by the live frame's own classes (`MediaPickerComponent`): the places
    (`FolderTreeComponent`, `mode: :picker`: a select below 640px, a 200px
    list from 640px), then the grid's column, which scrolls on its own.

    The marker carries the place's digest (`Media::Place#digest`), and the
    grid's column a slot above the grid, for the notice of
    `admin--media--live` on the dialog when another tab changed the place
    while the picker is open (the card's D13).

    In a folder's place, the folder's row above the grid (the card
    StudioGallery, D4): its mark, name and own kept images, and the button
    that adds its images to a gallery. Drawn `hidden`: only a multiple
    opening shows it, once `admin--media--picker` has asked its address
    (`GET /media_folders/:id/images`) and some image is new. %>
<turbo-frame id="media-picker-grid">
  <% place_name = @place.all? ? t(".place_all") : @place.none? ? t(".place_none") : @folder_tree.find(@place.folder).name %>
  <%= tag.div id: "media-picker-place", hidden: true, data: { media_place: @place.to_param, media_place_name: place_name, media_place_gone: @place_gone ? "" : nil,
                                                          media_place_digest: @place.digest(@folder_tree) } %>
  <%= render "admin/media/live_notice" %>
  <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::FolderTreeComponent.new(tree: @folder_tree, counts: @folder_counts, place: @place, query: @place_query,
        open_set: TreeOpenSet::EMPTY, manage: false, mode: :picker) %>

  <div class="min-h-0 overflow-y-auto px-6 py-4 sm:px-5">
    <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::ToolbarComponent.new(counts: @counts, filter: @search.filter, q: params[:q], url_options: admin_url_options, picker: true, place: (@place.to_param unless @place.all?)) %>

    <div data-admin--media--live-target="slot"></div>
    <% if @place.folder %>
      <% folder_count = @folder_counts[:folders].fetch(@place.folder, 0) %>
      <%= tag.div id: "media-picker-folder", hidden: true, class: "mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-2 text-sm text-ink",
                  data: { url: admin_media_folder_images_path(@place.folder, **admin_url_options) } do %>
        <%= render "admin/shared/icon", name: :folder, size: "size-4" %>
        <strong class="min-w-0 truncate font-semibold"><%= place_name %></strong>
        <span class="text-small text-meta"><%= t("admin.components.ui.media_picker.folder_count", count: folder_count) %></span>
        <%= render Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.new(label: t("admin.components.ui.media_picker.add_folder", count: folder_count), variant: :secondary, size: :small, type: "button",
              class: "ms-auto", data: { media_folder_add: true, action: "admin--media--picker#addFolder" }) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <% page_url = ->(page) { admin_media_path(list_params(:q, :filter, :picker, :folder).merge("page" => page)) } %>
    <% if @pagination.out_of_range? %>
      <%= render "admin/shared/out_of_range_page", url: page_url.call(1) %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::GridComponent.new(assets: @assets, url_options: admin_url_options, pick: true, locale: admin_locale) %>
      <% if @pagination.total_pages > 1 %>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-card bg-surface shadow-1">
          <%= render Admin::Ui::PaginationComponent.new(pagination: @pagination, url: page_url) %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</turbo-frame>
